What I like about the false rumors is they give useful context.  If a
false rumor says "You can't get by the snake", I know that I can get
by
Nethack snakes.  Maybe that's not usefull most of the time, but there
are Nethack monsters that do block the way.  And Nethack does have
polymorph.  Wanna bet if I polymorph that shopkeeper into a snake
he won't be able to block the door any more?

That's the art of the false rumors.  What they tell is false on the
surface,
but they give context of how to think to acheive results in Nethack.
If there's a false rumor that rust is permanent then I know there has
to
be a way ro repair rust.  If there's a false rumor that Medusa is vein
then I know to experiment with mirrors or reflection when facing her.

Discussion of how to apply the lesson of a true rumor is mildly
spoily.  Discussion of how to apply the lesson of a false rumor
is very spoily.

There is an additional reason for false rumors - Volume. The same
reason there are junk artifacts.  You eat the uncursed fortune cookie.
You get a false rumor.  Congratulations you are now the proud owner
of Ogresmasher a weapon so potent it is a gift from the devine.  Gee,
thanks.  This lesson gives yet another value to an item being blessed
or cursed or uncursed.  Want some usefull info?  Bless a fortune
cookie
before eating it.  Want some extremely obscure usefull info?  Curse a
fortune cookie before eating it.



